@startuml
title SIC/XE Assembler - High-Level Pipeline
left to right direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #455A64
  ArrowColor #546E7A
}

[*] --> Parse

state "Parse source\n\nparseLine per physical line\ncomments, fields, mnemonic, operands\nproduce Statement records + diagnostics" as Parse
state "Parsed statements\n\nSource order\nlabels, instruction/directive identity\noperand schema data" as IR
state "First stage (Pass 1)\n\nAssign addresses and sizes\nProcess layout directives\ndefine symbols\nvalidate address-space constraints" as Pass1
state "Second stage (Pass 2)\n\nResolve expression values\nprocess BASE / NOBASE / END\ncreate listing and relocation metadata" as Pass2
state "Instruction encoding\n\nFormat 1 / 2 / 3 / 4\nSIC or SIC/XE memory encoding\nvalidate field ranges and addressing" as Encode
state "Data encoding\n\nBYTE literals or values\nWORD 24-bit values + relocation" as Data
state "Assembly result\n\nsparse CodeMemory\nsymbols, entry point, length\nlisting, relocations, diagnostics" as Result

Parse --> IR
IR --> Pass1
Pass1 --> Pass2
Pass2 --> Encode : instruction
Pass2 --> Data : BYTE / WORD
Encode --> Result
Data --> Result
Result --> [*]

note bottom of Pass1
Each assembly run owns its own Engine state.
The parser builds Statements before either pass begins.
end note
@enduml
